\series bold
c
\series default
.
 If 
\begin_inset Formula $a:=-\pi$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $b:=\pi$
\end_inset

,
 the series becomes 
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{\pi-(-\pi)}{2\pi}+\sum_{k\ne0}\frac{\exp(ik\pi)-\exp(-ik\pi)}{2\pi ik}=\frac{2\pi}{2\pi}+\sum_{k\ne0}\frac{0}{2\pi ik}=1$
\end_inset

.
 
